 ## Background
-The NDC Ray Transformation was introduced in the NeRF paper (Mildenhall et al., 2020) to handle real-world forward-facing captures where the scene extends to infinity [S1]. It adapts the normalized device coordinates used in triangle rasterization pipelines to neural radiance fields, mapping the perspective rays to parallel rays in the transformed volume and using disparity instead of metric depth [S1]. This allows the neural network to learn a bounded representation for unbounded scenes.
+The NDC Ray Transformation was introduced in the NeRF paper (Mildenhall et al., 2020) to handle real-world forward-facing captures where the scene extends to infinity [S1]. It adapts the normalized device coordinates used in triangle rasterization pipelines to neural radiance fields, mapping the perspective rays to parallel rays in the transformed volume and using disparity instead of metric depth [S1]. This allows the neural network to learn a bounded representation for unbounded scenes [S1].
 
